==Personality==
{{Quote|Eon wants nothing less than absolute power over everything. All timelines; all alternate realities; '''[[Multiverse|everything]]'''.|[[Professor Paradox]], explaining Eon's motivations.<ref name="BA" />}}
Eon is essentially a psychopath. He is willing to mess up the timelines just to get what he wants, and would resort to destroying all of existence if denied the chance to rule.<ref name="BA">''[[Ben Again]]''</ref> Eon can be dangerously cunning and manipulative in combat, waiting throughout the physical fighting until the time is right for him to make a climactic move.

Eon can be very bloodthirsty, as when he thought that [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] was going to use his [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]] to erase [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] and his entire [[No Watch Timeline|timeline]], he was impressed and said, "''Nice!''".<ref name="ATTWN">''[[And Then There Were None]]''</ref>

Eon apparently has a long history with and a deep hatred of [[Professor Paradox]], to whom he is in many ways equal yet inferior; while Eon can be very intelligent and can perceive the fragility of spacetime, unlike Paradox, he fails to recognize that the fullest power of a nigh-omnipotent device such as the [[Chrononavigator]] is not something that can be exploited and controlled without cataclysmic consequences.<ref name="BA" />

Eon is willing to work with other villains when their goals will benefit him in some way, but unfortunately for him, he fails to realize that the most evil and intelligent of said villains may have treacherous hidden agendas. These would have a detrimental effect on him once his usefulness has ended.<ref name="TEoaE">''[[The End of an Era]]''</ref>

Eon fails to learn this from previous double-crossings that have happened to him; this was what allowed Vilgax to manipulate him during their partnership to wipe out the good Bens across the multiverse, with fatal consequences for Eon himself.<ref name="ATTWN" />

Eon does not appreciate being backstabbed, upon being restored from erasure by No Watch Ben as [[Clockwork]], he immediately attacked Vilgax for playing and ultimately erasing him.<ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref>

==History==
===Background===
<tabber>
|-|Canon Version=
Eon is an alternate reality counterpart of [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Tennyson]] who became corrupted and evil at some point in his life. Like most of his other counterparts, he originally had his own [[Omnitrix]]. However, something bad happened which resulted in the device being destroyed. Eon would integrate the leftover parts from his Omnitrix into the gauntlet on his left arm.{{Refn|[[:File:Eon's Omnitrix.png]]|name = OM|group = DJW}}

Travelling to the [[Race Against Time Timeline]], Eon arrived on [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]] 200 years ago to activate the [[Hands of Armageddon]] and start an interdimensional invasion. However, he was captured by the first Earth [[Plumbers (Classic)|Plumbers]]{{Refn|[[:File:Eon First Appearance.png]]|group = pop-up|name = debut}}<ref name="RAT" /> and placed in cryogenic freezing for 200 years. Eon would eventually break out in the present day and aged his guardian [[Constantine Jacobs]] to near-death. Unbeknownst to this timeline's [[Ben Tennyson (Race Against Time Timeline)|Ben Tennyson]], some of Eon's previous attempts to control him were thwarted by [[Professor Paradox]].{{Refn|[[:File:Paradox vs Eon RAT.png]]|group = pop-up|name = Paradox}}<ref name="RAT" />
|-|Retconned Version=<br>
Eon was a [[Chronian]] who escaped the interdimensional entrapment of his species. Intend on freeing his people back into the universe at any cost, he arrived on [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]] 200 years ago to activate the [[Hands of Armageddon]] and start the Chronians' invasion. However, he was captured by the first Earth [[Plumbers (Classic)|Plumbers]]{{Refn|[[:File:Eon First Appearance.png]]|group = pop-up|name = debut}}<ref name="RAT" /> and placed in cryogenic freezing for 200 years. Eon would eventually break out in the present day and aged his guardian [[Constantine Jacobs]] to near-death. Unbeknowst to [[Ben Tennyson (Race Against Time Timeline)|Ben Tennyson]], some of Eon's previous attempts to control him were thwarted by [[Professor Paradox]].{{Refn|[[:File:Paradox vs Eon RAT.png]]|group = pop-up|name = Paradox}}<ref name="RAT" />
</tabber>

===Ben 10===
Eon first appeared in '''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time]]''''', where he went searching for the Hands with the help of warriors from throughout time that he turned into abnormal creatures that would act as his [[Eon's Minions (Race Against Time)|minions]].{{Refn|[[:File:RAT Eon's Minions.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="RAT" /> Finding out that he was too old and weak to activate the Hands, he set about capturing [[Ben Tennyson (Race Against Time Timeline)|Ben Tennyson]], with the intention of using his [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] to turn his counterpart into a [[Eon (Transformation)|younger clone of himself]]. To ensure the transformation would be complete, Eon deactivated a failsafe so that his DNA would completely overtake the younger Ben's personality. Due to his powers over matter, Eon's personality persisted in the sampled DNA.{{Refn|[[:File:Eon Retain Personality.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="RAT" /> Upon succeeding in this goal, the elder Eon seemingly wiped himself from existence to prevent two versions of himself from existing in the same world.

As the younger Eon, Ben activated the Hands of Armageddon. However, his human personality retook control when [[Gwen Tennyson (Race Against Time Timeline)|Gwen]] managed to reach her cousin inside the younger Eon, prompting him to revert back to human. Meanwhile, [[Max Tennyson (Race Against Time Timeline)|Max]] deactivated the Hands, thwarting the elder Eon's invasion. Returning to existence, the real Eon tried to exact his revenge. However, Ben as [[Wildmutt]] managed to send Eon crashing into the Hands of Armageddon, destroying it in a huge explosion of bright, glowing purple energy. Though he believed Eon had been destroyed with the Hands, Ben had inadvertently sent Eon out of his timeline and into [[Multiverse|cross-time]], something [[Professor Paradox]] became aware of.

===Ultimate Alien===
[[File:B10kR (69).png|thumb|left|Eon vs Ultimate Ben as Clockwork|218x218px]]
After winding up in crosstime, Eon began travelling through many other timelines. Whenever he crossed paths with a different version of himself, he would absorb and enslave the resident Ben Tennyson of whatever timeline he traveled to, turning them into [[Eon's Minions (Ben 10,000 Returns)|new minions]] under his control. Eon's ultimate intention was to absorb several Bens Tennysons to have enough power to replace the Prime timeline with a new one, where he would be the only Ben Tennyson, and absorbing Ben Prime or his future self would give Eon the power to finally accomplish his goal.

In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Eon travelled to the [[Ultimate Alien Future Timeline]] and broke into [[Tennyson Tower|Ben 10,000's headquarters]] where he and his minions fought the resident [[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|Ben 10,000]]. Turning into [[Ultimate Ben]], Ben 10,000 used [[Clockwork]]'s abilities to send Eon 20 years earlier to '''Ultimate Alien'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s timeframe, unaware that Eon needed that to happen in order to complete his plan. Eon created a trap by using the [[Prime Timeline]]'s Hand of Armageddon, which was stored in a [[Bellwood (Classic)|Bellwood]] museum, to emit a signal that the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] would pick up. When [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] touched the Hands of Armageddon, the artifact sent a pulse into the device, allowing Eon's minions to travel through and fight Ben, [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]], and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]]. After Eon’s minions were defeated, they were sent back once again.

After the Hands of Armageddon were strapped inside the [[Rustbucket 3]], Eon's minions once again fought the team. The minions managed to damage the Rustbucket 3, forcing the ship to plummet down to the surface. When Ben as [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]] and Ultimate Ben as Clockwork attempted to destroy the Hands of Armageddon, they unintentionally allowed Eon and his minions to break out. Eon used his time rays to age Way Big to dust, seemingly killing Ben. However, Eon merely destroyed the transformation and not Ben himself. From there, a battle erupted between Eon's forces and Ben's team.

After swiping Ben 10,000 off to the side, Eon shoots his beams of energy towards [[Ultimate Swampfire]], but only manages to age the seedlings that he planted before vanishing. This leaves Eon confused, allowing Ultimate Swampfire to grab Eon, demanding an explanation for his actions. Eon says that their paths are intertwined in every timeline. Eon managed to get the upper hand by throwing Ultimate Swampfire to the ground and aging both the transformation and his [[Swampfire|regular counterpart]], leaving Ben vulnerable. Before Eon could finish Ben off, he was saved by Ultimate Ben, who protected himself from Eon's beams by forming a manna shield in front of him and escapes along with Ben.

[[File:B10kR (523).png|thumb|right|Eon defeated|218x218px]]
After the gang had discovered that Eon's minions are actually alternate Bens when Gwen immobilizes them, Eon explained his plan to absorb both Ben and Ben 10,000 so he can replace the current timeline with a new one. Taking his helmet off, he revealed his identity as an alternate Ben 10,000 and was confronted by [[Professor Paradox]]. Eon tells the time walker that he cannot interfere, yet Paradox understood this and says that if Eon were to proceed with his plans, he will have no place to hide. Ben discovered that Eon never came through the Hands of Armageddon, but rather through their respective Ultimatrixes, and that through the whole fight Eon was luring all of them away from the artifact. Eon attempts to age Ben to dust once again, but Ben manages to transform into [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]] and flies towards the Hands of Armageddon. Gwen, Kevin, and Ben 10,000 fight off Eon while Jetray destroys the Hands of Armageddon, causing Eon to explode. Paradox stated that all the Bens Eon had controlled would go back to their own timelines and return to normal.

===Omniverse===
[[File:Ben10OVbenagain (163).png|thumb|left|Eon vs Paradox|218x218px]]
Despite his demise, Eon reappeared, yet ended up trapped in the main timeline by Paradox. Seeking to get hold of the time-walker's [[Chrononavigator]] in order to have the freedom to traverse the multiverse once more, Eon went after Ben both when he was 11 and when he is 16 at the same time. He also acquired [[Eon's Minions (Omniverse)|new minions]] in the form of robots.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Eon's Servants Robots.png]]|group = DJW}}

In ''[[Ben Again]]'', Eon battles both Bens in their respective time zones before touching their [[Omnitrix]]es, causing the immature 11-year-old Ben to switch minds with his more mature 16-year-old self. Realizing Paradox wouldn't show up in the present day because the 11-year-old mind of Ben doesn't know him, Eon quickly went to 11-year-old Ben's time zone, where he ambushed Paradox and cut off his robotic right hand.

Eon held Paradox captive in the [[End of Time|end of time]]{{Refn|[[:File:Eon Trapped Paradox at the End of Time.png]]|group = DJW}} for interrogation and, knowing that Paradox never lies, figured out that his missing cybernetic hand was his Chrononavigator. Originally planning to go back to the moment it was severed, Eon was warned against doing so by Paradox as it risked throwing him out of existence due to the fabric of reality being stretched thin by both of their presences and the switched minds of Ben.

[[File:BA 477.PNG|thumb|Almost defeated|218x218px]]
Eon instead went to the present day, where he stole the Chrononavigator from the immature Ben once he found it. Eon used the Chrononavigator to summon his minions, but Eon's abuse of the device's power began to seriously stretch and damage the fabric of time. As both the present and 11-year-old Ben's time were now visible through the distortions Eon had created, Eon was blasted out of the timeline by the 11-year-old and 16-year-old Bens' versions of Clockwork, restoring reality to normal and erasing all the events he had just caused to occur.

[[File:ATTWN (267).png|thumb|left|Eon with Vilgax and the evil Bens|218x218px]]
In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', Eon joined forces with [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] to, as Eon believed, create an army of evil Omnitrix-wielders under Vilgax's control, which Eon achieved through gathering an army of evil Ben Tennysons from all across the multiverse and destroying those among the alternate Bens who refused to join. After Vilgax and Eon had five evil versions of Ben- [[Albedo]], [[Bad Ben]], [[Mad Ben|Mad Ben]], [[Benzarro]], and [[Nega Ben]]- under their control, they went to the [[No Watch Timeline]], with Eon and the evil Bens intending to destroy [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] since his reality's lack of an Omnitrix made it an unpredictable temporal wildcard. However, while Eon and the evil Bens were fighting against a team of benevolent Omnitrix-wielders gathered by Professor Paradox to counter them, Vilgax betrayed Eon. Using a [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]], Vilgax wiped all the other timelines, and their respective Omnitrix-wielders with them, from spacetime, Eon included.

[[File:ATTWN (411).png|thumb|Eon getting wiped from spacetime|218x218px]]
In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', Eon was seen in the recent past in [[Dimension 23]], back when he was still recruiting alternate Bens for his and Vilgax's army. Eon was fighting [[Ben 23]] for refusing to join, but with [[Gwen 10 (Gweniverse)|Gwen 10]] and present No Watch Ben's unseen help, Ben 23 defeated Eon and forced him to flee to another dimension in search of more persuadable Bens. After Vilgax had successfully deployed the Chronosapien Time Bomb back in the present, Eon was brought back into existence when No Watch Ben used Clockwork to suck the Time Bomb's ripple back in. He attacked Vilgax and tried to finish him off for backstabbing him, but before he could have done it, [[Fourmungousaur]] swatted him away. At the end of the episode, he was sent to his own timeline by Clockwork.

[[File:LDtTWA (281).png|thumb|Eon with a Time Beast|left|218x218px]]
In ''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]'', Eon was sent by [[Maltruant]] to collect the eggs of a [[Time Beast]] to aid him in the [[Time War]]. Eon met up with [[Exo-Skull]] and [[Subdora]] to get the eggs but ran into difficulty with Ben and [[Rook Blonko]]'s interference. Even more, Paradox and [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] appeared to help stop Eon as well. Eon eventually released a Time Beast and Ben and Rook are forced to try and stop it. Eon mainly fought with Paradox and summoned his minions to fight Ben 10,000. Eon then managed to escape with two Time Beast eggs and deliver them to Maltruant.

In ''[[The End of an Era]]'', Eon was summoned to Ben 10,000's timeline by Maltruant, bringing with him a Time Beast-pulled chariot. Maltruant pushed Eon off the chariot, telling him that his services were no longer required. Eon was angered, saying they had a deal. Maltruant responded by nonchalantly sending Eon back to his own timeline.

