==Etymology==
An eon is a time measurement unit that involves multiple eras and is equal to one billion years.

==Trivia==
*Eon was meant to be a scarfaced young man with gravestone teeth, greasy hairline, dark helmet and wearing an overcoat.{{Refn|[[:File:HoA 1.png]]|group=script}}<ref>'''''[[Ben 10 and the Hands of Armageddon]]'''''</ref>
*Much like [[Professor Paradox]], it is hard to tell exactly what order events occur from Eon's perspective due to his ability to travel through time.
**As such, it is unknown if Eon actually died in ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'' after being defeated (as evidenced by Paradox saying that he was "no more") and if his appearances in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' are from his past.
*Unlike some of Ben's alternate counterparts, Eon's [[Omnitrix]] did not have a unique name.{{Refn|group = DJW|[[:File:Eon's Omnitrix Does Not Have A Special Name.png]]}}
*Eon and [[Malware]] are the only known characters in the classic continuity who have the ability to directly destroy [[Omnitrix]] transformations.
*[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] developed a backstory for Eon that he belongs to a timeline that branched off from a 20-year-old Ben Prime, though this idea was not used during the show's run.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 100.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Derrick would have liked to have explored Eon's story in the series.{{Refn|[[:File:EonUnknown.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Eon's portrayal in '''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time|Race Against Time]]''''' was partially inspired by [[wikipedia:Darth Vader|Darth Vader]] from the '''[[wikipedia:Star Wars|Star Wars]]''' franchise. [[Christien Anholt]] seemed eager to portray Eon because he is a fan of Darth Vader.{{Refn|https://archive.is/6jTLJ|group = CA}}
*Eon's Omniverse design was done by [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] and [[Chap Yaep]] with Chris Hooten.{{Refn|[[:File:Time Warriors OV design credits .png]]|name = Time|group = DJW}} 

